resizeListenT -- forms step 6, stroke 4 (2026-11-12): the resize arriving by listening. Kant only; no engine change beyond
Tony's runNotified of that day (a listener's own action fires when its notifier is written).

The shape: layoutFrame is a field outside the form holding x y width height -- the request's frame:=. onResize listens to
it, and its action calls redrawForm(request), which lays the form out afresh through setFrame and writes the PDF.
    Writing the frame's width and height (:% replaces an attribute) notifies nobody: an attribute is its own field, and
    layoutFrame's listeners hang on layoutFrame. So the four values can be written one by one and the form is not laid out
    four times.
    One write to layoutFrame's own value (layoutFrame = 1) is the command: it fires onResize once.
That second line is a choice made here to get a first run, not a ruling: "fire on demand" is Tony's to design.

Rows in genLadder/formsPop.sh. The form is IncantForms/Windows/simple and the points are resizeT's, so the two roads can be
read against each other: a resize by listening must read as resizeT's plain call does.
